      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-104012",
      ":question/problem": "The vector-valued function $f(\u03b8, \u03d5)$, given by\n\n$f(\u03b8, \u03d5) = \u27e82\\sinh \u03d5\\cos \u03b8, _____, 2\\cosh \u03d5\u27e9$\n\nparametrizes one sheet of the hyperboloid of two sheets defined in Cartesian coordinates as $x^{2} + y^{2} - z^{2} =-4$. By expressing the equation of the hyperboloid in cylindrical polar coordinates, determine the second component of $f$.\n\n*Hint: You may use the fact that the hyperbola $z^{2} - r^{2} = k^{2}$ can be parametrized as $\u27e8z, r\u27e9 = \u27e8k\\cosh \u03d5, k\\sinh \u03d5\u27e9$* for $\u03d5 \u2208 R$."
